%% aoneahsan-cccs-fileshub-vault — full flow
flowchart TD
    trigger([Need a project credential]) --> where{Running server-side<br/>or CLI/agent?}
    where -->|browser or a repo| stop[STOP — the fh_pat_ token is<br/>account-wide and the plane sends<br/>no CORS. Secrets store only]
    where -->|yes| introspect[GET /token FIRST.<br/>Four of the five scopes<br/>are OFF by default]

    introspect --> scoped{Does the token hold<br/>the scope this vault needs?}
    scoped -->|no — 403 TOKEN_PERMISSION_DENIED| askowner[Only the owner can grant a scope,<br/>in Nova. PAUSE and ask.<br/>Do NOT fall back to guessing.<br/>NB the 403 may name a friendly<br/>label, not the Nova field]
    scoped -->|yes| which{What are you<br/>looking for?}

    which -->|"a project's third-party<br/>credentials or config files"| registry[GET /vault/services — the registry,<br/>no scope needed. Read it before<br/>guessing a field name]
    registry --> detail[GET /projects/p/vault<br/>has.* presence flags, no values]
    detail --> populated{Any configured<br/>service?}

    populated -->|"no — now the RARE case:<br/>3 of 55 projects since 2026-08-20"| empty[EMPTY is NOT 'not applicable'.<br/>Report 'the vault has nothing stored',<br/>fall back to ~/.secrets, and WRITE it<br/>over the Management API — since<br/>2026.08.20.1 this is no longer<br/>owner-only Nova work]
    populated -->|"yes — the normal case:<br/>52 of 55 projects"| reveal[POST .../vault/reveal<br/>values + env blocks + undecryptable.<br/>Add /service to narrow it]
    reveal --> envblock[Use the env block AS GIVEN.<br/>vite and next carry only client_safe<br/>fields — hand-filtering re-opens the<br/>server-secret hole. Empty blocks<br/>are dropped, so env {} is normal]
    envblock --> filesq{Need the file itself?}
    filesq -->|yes| files[GET .../vault-files/service.key<br/>raw bytes + X-Checksum-Sha256.<br/>NOT vault/files/...]
    filesq -->|no| handle
    files --> handle

    which -->|"hosted Supabase"| task{Which Supabase task?}
    task -->|"app runtime or<br/>db push migrations"| proj[POST /supabase-projects/ref/reveal<br/>DB password + session pooler.<br/>Substitute the password into the URL,<br/>percent-encoded — the stored one is a<br/>YOUR-PASSWORD placeholder]
    task -->|"functions deploy,<br/>secrets set, link"| acct[POST /supabase-accounts/idOrEmail/reveal<br/>the sbp_ PAT + env.cli.<br/>The PROJECT vault has no access_token<br/>and never will]
    proj --> handle
    acct --> handle

    handle[Never echo a revealed value —<br/>pipe it where it belongs.<br/>undecryptable means re-enter in Nova,<br/>not unset. Every reveal is recorded]
    handle --> gate{Capability built<br/>recently?}
    gate -->|yes| version[curl /api/version — a feature exists<br/>only after the owner deploys, and the<br/>repo CHANGELOG has been wrong about<br/>this before]
    gate -->|no| done
    version --> done([Record where the credential landed;<br/>report honestly what the vault<br/>actually returned])

    empty --> done
    askowner --> done

    classDef gateNode fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#d97706,color:#7c2d12
    classDef stopNode fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#7f1d1d
    classDef terminal fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b
    class where,scoped,which,populated,filesq,task,gate gateNode
    class stop,empty,askowner stopNode
    class trigger,done terminal
